The routine alg-s computes the antilogarithm of a three-digit mantissa, by pseudo-multiplication, the exponent
rescaled each level.

Input: a mantissa m from 0 to 999. Result: 100 times 10 to the power m / 1000, rounded, from 100 to 998: the three
significant digits of the antilogarithm, whose characteristic places the decimal point. A logarithm L = 1000c + m
gives the number s times 10 to the power c - 2.

Call: load m into the accumulator and JMP 12. It returns with the result in the accumulator.
Cells 12-98 (87 cells). It writes cell 99 and, of its own cells, 33, 41, 52, 61-66, 98; nothing else.
Cost: at most 911 instructions a call, 525.3 on average over the domain, counted from its first cell to its return
jump. Worst error: 2 in the last digit (units of the third significant digit) against the correctly rounded value,
at m = 965; 269 of the 1,000 inputs are off.
Address bases: cell 53 holds SUB 56. To move the routine down by d cells, subtract d from every address in its
instructions that points into cells 12-98 and from the address bases; addresses 00 and 99 stay as they are.

